PATCH 475: FUN_1000_a930 -- the swept proximity test froze the engine (an uninitialised `unaff_CS` used as
the loop counter) and truncated its 32-bit coordinates to 16 bits.

asm 0x1a930-0x1a9b8 (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00): march the moving object along its velocity for 24 steps
(`mov cx,0x18` ... `push cx` / `pop cx` / `loop`), each step advancing dword[0x9684]/[0x9688] by
dword[0x9962]/[0x9966] (mirrored into 0xe444/0xe44c) and testing 0927's range via a19a against the
combined radius word[0x979e] = word[si+0x14] + word[di+0x14] + word[0x97a0]; `jbe` -> STC (hit), loop
exhausted -> CLC.  Ghidra bound the `pop cx` counter to the uninitialised pseudo-var `unaff_CS`
(`iVar2 = unaff_CS - 1; unaff_CS = 0;`), so the counter ran 0x18, garbage-1, -1, -1 ... and the loop never
ended: with the corrected object spawns (patch 462) the AZER1 self-play reached this path at t=16988 and
the engine stopped inside a single c0e5 object walk (the frame counter [0x6cde] frozen at 37484, the
cooperative tick starved).  It also wrote the routine's 32-bit position words through the 2-byte
DAT_2000_* accessors, truncating every coordinate.  Rebuilt 1:1 at the asm widths with the CF result
threaded via g_fist_cf (a0ab's `jb` consumes it).

Shim (tools/native_main.c): the cooperative-tick MISSION WINDOW is now sticky -- the pre-cockpit load
phase is still held (both targets), but once the cockpit view has been entered the PIT keeps running for
the rest of the mission.  The old `d549 == 0x1c` gate froze [0x452] the moment the engine switched to
another mission viewport (0x1e/0x20/0x22), which stopped time in exactly the frames this patch unblocks.
